# Absence drops out of a plain list and is REFUSED under a spread:
# `x: ["a", maybe($.gone)]` alone is {"x":["a"]}, and the same list
# under `[&: string]` is listval_no_gen. Both ports agree on THIS
# shape, so it is a design gap. Swap the template for `string|number`
# and they stop agreeing -- see test/spec/divergent.tsv. Run:
#   aontu absent-under-a-spread.aontu
# The same shape inside aontu:code's decls is func_arity, which is
# what stops a heading vanishing with the rows it heads (ADR-037).
# expected: {"x":["a"]}
# actual:   [aontu/listval_no_gen] at $.x.1
x: [&: string]

x: ["a" maybe($.gone)]
